 @jirosaves_theworld  seems fine to me! In January 2021; £200 delivered next day in UK from Amazon.

For my R3/16GB tower 5500XT makes the most sense for my 450W power supply...

Performs great would recommend.

 @masterkairiZ  Dude, I'm an Nvidia fanboy, I've had Nvidia cards since GeForce 2 on my Hercules 3D Profit card.

But that doesn't negate the fact that AMD cards are generally a good value and can do almost anything an Nvidia card can do… including streaming games. Maybe your settings are messed up, maybe the rest of your computer is a potato, maybe you have bad internet, or maybe you just lost the silicon lottery and got a bad card, but it doesn't mean all the 5500xt's are bad.

Though it has been 3-years since I posted my original comment so there are also LOTS of new cards out there and it might just be time for an upgrade for you.

 @lorsch.  I returned my Asus Strix 5700 XT lol... out of the box it needs undervolt which is ok-ish... but hell after an entire day of trying to get rid of random micro stutters and freezes of 5 seconds every 20-30 mins, I decided to return it. Ended up reinstalling Windows with fresh clean AMD drivers just to experience the same crap. The card was pulling awesome fps at 1440p... but AMD drivers are still having issues.

ALSO: Same issue with the screws. Can't be arsed to pay almost 500 euro for a card just to tweak it around and hope for drive fixes. Gonna buy 2070 SUPER, ain't gonna get rich with extra 70 bucks.

EDIT: Imagine that I upgraded from a 1060 6GB which had significantly lower fps but never freezes or stutters.

